The 100th celebration of the Macy's Thanksgiving Day Parade in New York City is finding itself at the mercy of the weather gods. It's made it through rain and even snow, but this time it's facing an incoming storm that is threatening to bring heavy winds. If things get too windy, the iconic balloons could be grounded.

This would mark the first time since 1971 that the balloons would be grounded. Related Stories 'Jimmy' Review: Cornball James Stewart Biopic Gets the Manner, but Not the Man ‘Best Pancakes in the County’ Review: Nicolas Cage Stars in a Thriller You Could Fairly Describe as Tarantino Lite

Balloons are grounded when sustained winds reach 24 mph or wind gusts reach 35 mph. Any decisions regarding balloon flight will be made on parade morning and will be based on weather conditions. blogherads.adq.push(function () { blogherads .defineSlot( 'medrec', 'gpt-variety-article-mid-article-uid0' ) .setTargeting( 'pos', ["mid-article1","mid-articleX","mid","mid-article"] ) .setTargeting( 'viewable', 'yes' ) .setSubAdUnitPath("ros\/mid-article") .addSize([[300,250],[2,2],[300,251],[2,4],[4,2],[320,480],[620,366],[300,450]]) .setClsOptimization("minsize") ; });

NBC is closely monitoring the weather forecast, with safety being its top priority.

As previously reported , this year's parade is titled &#x201C;The Greatest Celebration,&#x201D; in honor of its centennial anniversary with over 100 floats and 100 balloons.

Among the balloons that are set to take flight are Sorcerer&#x2019;s Apprentice Mickey and Joe Cool.

&#x201C;It&#x2019;s a massive deal for the folks at Disney,&#x201D; Brendan Kennedy, director of creative production at Macy&#x2019;s Studio told Variety . &#x201C;It&#x2019;s not an IP that generally comes out, except for a huge celebration. It&#x2019;s our 100th parade, and they were really excited to join us. It was just a joy to get close to Mickey, but the Sorcerer&#x2019;s Apprentice is so special. It&#x2019;s that next level of elevated magic that blends really well with Macy&#x2019;s.&#x201D;

Another highlight is Snoopy, who returns to the parade in a new role as Joe Cool. &#x201C;Joe Cool is what happens when Snoopy is pretending to be a student at school. He&#x2019;s never been in the parade before in this form, which makes it really fun,&#x201D; Kennedy said. &#x201C;We&#x2019;re excited to bring him and Woodstock together. I was on the Parade Studio floor yesterday and saw an arm and an ear being worked on.&#x201D;

Steven Hack, an original cast member in the Broadway production of &#x201C; Cats &#x201D; who appeared in TV series including " American Horror Story ," died Nov. 19 in Los Angeles following a "sudden and unexpected cardiac event," Interact Theatre Company confirmed on social media. He was 68.

Hack performed and understudied in multiple roles in "Cats," including Mungojerrie, Carbucketty, Coricopat, Pouncival and Tumblebrutus. Related Stories 'NCIS: New York' Sells Across 135 Markets Globally (EXCLUSIVE) How to Watch President Trump's '60 Minutes' Interview Online Free

&#x201C;It is with great sadness that we share the news that Steven Hack, a founding member of Interact Theatre Company, recently passed away at home following a sudden and unexpected cardiac event,&#x201D; the company wrote on Instagram . blogherads.adq.push(function () { blogherads .defineSlot( 'medrec', 'gpt-variety-article-mid-article-uid0' ) .setTargeting( 'pos', ["mid-article1","mid-articleX","mid","mid-article"] ) .setTargeting( 'viewable', 'yes' ) .setSubAdUnitPath("ros\/mid-article") .addSize([[300,250],[2,2],[300,251],[2,4],[4,2],[320,480],[620,366],[300,450]]) .setClsOptimization("minsize") ; });

The post continued, &#x201C;Steven was a gifted and versatile performer, a superb graphic artist and a cherished member of our artistic family. His creativity and talent helped shape Interact in its earliest years, and his artistry, humor, warmth and generous spirit enriched everything he touched.&#x201D;

In addition to &#x201C;Cats,&#x201D; Hack had an extensive career as an actor with roles in &#x201C;American Horror Story,&#x201D; &#x201C;Ratched,&#x201D; &#x201C;Marvel&#x2019;s Agent Carter,&#x201D; "Days of Our Lives" and &#x201C;General Hospital.&#x201D; Other roles included "Amsterdam," "Angelyne," "Pam and Tommy" and "The West Wing."

He was born in St. Louis before attending college at the California Institute of the Arts and the American Academy of Dramatic Arts. He made his professional debut as one of the teenage dancers in the 1978 film &#x201C;Grease&#x201D; before heading to Broadway and accruing a long list of film and television titles.

The company concluded its post, &#x201C;As we remember Steven, we celebrate not only his many contributions to our company but also the joy of knowing and working with him. He will always hold a special place in Interact&#x2019;s history and in the hearts of those who knew him. We extend our heartfelt condolences to his family, friends and all who loved him. May his memory be a blessing.&#x201D;

As the nation remains enthralled by Nathan Fielder and Lance Oppenheim&#x2019;s Elizabeth Holmes film &#x201C;You Can See Everything,&#x201D; the first documentary to cross $100 million at the global box office in over two decades, arguably the most influential &#x2014; and the most prolific &#x2014; documentarian in American cinema&#x2019;s works have found a new home.

The complete works of Frederick Wiseman , the renowned documentary filmmaker behind &#x201C;Titicut Follies&#x201D; (1967), &#x201C;Hospital&#x201D; (1970) and &#x201C;Ex Libris: The New York Public Library&#x201D; (2017), have found a home with Janus Films . Wiseman produced, directed and edited 45 features that were released under Zipporah Films, Inc., his production and distribution company named for his wife, and they&#x2019;ll all be distributed by Janus Films in North America starting Jan. 1, 2027, joining an impressive library that includes films by greats like Agn&#xE8;s Varda, Ingmar Bergman, Akira Kurosawa and Chantal Akerman. blogherads.adq.push(function () { blogherads .defineSlot( 'medrec', 'gpt-variety-article-mid-article-uid0' ) .setTargeting( 'pos', ["mid-article1","mid-articleX","mid","mid-article"] ) .setTargeting( 'viewable', 'yes' ) .setSubAdUnitPath("ros\/mid-article") .addSize([[300,250],[2,2],[300,251],[2,4],[4,2],[320,480],[620,366],[300,450]]) .setClsOptimization("minsize") ; }); Related Stories 'NCIS: New York' Sells Across 135 Markets Globally (EXCLUSIVE) Tony Awards Will Remain on CBS Through 2032 Under New Five-Year Deal

Wiseman&#x2019;s early films, from &#x201C;Titicut Follies&#x201D; (1967) through &#x201C;State Legislature&#x201D; (2007), will be available in 4K (having been restored by Zipporah Films), while &#x201C;La Danse&#x201D; (2009) through &#x201C;Menus-Plaisirs &#x2014; Les Troisgros&#x201D; (2023) will be offered in their original digital formats. &#x201C;A director whose rigorously objective explorations of social institutions constitute one of the most revered bodies of work in American documentary filmmaking,&#x201D; according to The New York Times, Wiseman, who passed away earlier this year at the age of 96, crafted a one-of-a-kind filmography that chronicled the experiences of everyday people in the U.S. (and France). He was given the Honorary Award for lifetime achievement from the Academy of Motion Picture Arts and Sciences in 2016, and his works helped expose corruption in vulnerable communities. blogherads.adq.push(function () { blogherads .defineSlot( 'medrec', 'gpt-dsk-tab-mid-article2-uid1' ) .setTargeting( 'pos', ["mid","mid-article2","mid-articleX"] ) .setTargeting( 'viewable', 'yes' ) .setSubAdUnitPath("ros\/mid-article2") .addSize([[320,480],[300,250],[300,251],[2,4],[4,2],[620,366],[300,450]]) .setClsOptimization("minsize") ; });

&#x201C;We couldn&#x2019;t imagine a better home in North America for Frederick Wiseman&#x2019;s films than with Janus Films,&#x201D; said Karen Konicek of Zipporah Films. &#x201C;It has been an honor to work alongside Fred for so many decades, producing and distributing his films. As Zipporah Films continues as the rights holder and distributor of the Wiseman Collection, we very much look forward to this new partnership with Janus Films and are excited to collaborate with them.&#x201D;

&#x201C;We are honored and thrilled to be the first distributor, in the U.S., outside of Zipporah Films, to be entrusted with licensing one of the greatest bodies of work in American cinema&#x201D; said Peter Becker, President of Janus Films and Criterion. &#x201C;We&#x2019;re looking forward to presenting these monumental works, theatrically, to new audiences across the country.&#x201D;

The full list of titles acquired: &#x201C;Titicut Follies&#x201D; (1967), &#x201C;High School&#x201D; (1968,) &#x201C;Law and Order&#x201D; (1969), &#x201C;Hospital&#x201D; (1970), &#x201C;Basic Training&#x201D; (1971), &#x201C;Essene&#x201D; (1972), &#x201C;Juvenile Court&#x201D; (1973), &#x201C;Primate&#x201D; (1974), &#x201C;Welfare&#x201D; (1975), &#x201C;Meat&#x201D; (1976), &#x201C;Canal Zone&#x201D; (1977), &#x201C;Sinai Field Mission&#x201D; (1978), &#x201C;Manoeuvre&#x201D; (1979), &#x201C;Model&#x201D; (1980), &#x201C;The Store&#x201D; (1983), &#x201C;Racetrack&#x201D; (1985), &#x201C;Blind&#x201D; (1986), &#x201C;Deaf&#x201D;(1986), &#x201C;Adjustment & Work&#x201D; (1986), &#x201C;Multi-handicapped&#x201D; (1986), &#x201C;Missile&#x201D; (1988), &#x201C;Near Death&#x201D; (1989), &#x201C;Central Park&#x201D; (1990), &#x201C;Aspen&#x201D; (1991), &#x201C;Zoo&#x201D; (1993), &#x201C;High School II&#x201D; (1994), &#x201C;Ballet&#x201D; (1995), &#x201C;La Com&#xE9;die-Fran&#xE7;aise ou L'amour jou&#xE9;&#x201D; (1996), &#x201C;Public Housing&#x201D; (1997), &#x201C;Belfast, Maine&#x201D; (1999), &#x201C;Domestic Violence&#x201D; (2001), &#x201C;Domestic Violence 2&#x201D; (2002), &#x201C;The Last Letter&#x201D; (2002), &#x201C;State Legislature&#x201D; (2007), &#x201C;La Danse: The Paris Opera Ballet&#x201D; (2009), &#x201C;Boxing Gym&#x201D; (2010), &#x201C;Crazy Horse&#x201D; (2011), &#x201C;At Berkeley&#x201D; (2013), &#x201C;National Gallery&#x201D; (2014), &#x201C;In Jackson Heights&#x201D; (2015), &#x201C;Ex Libris: The New York Public Library&#x201D; (2017), &#x201C;Monrovia, Indiana&#x201D; (2018), &#x201C;City Hall&#x201D; (2020), &#x201C;A Couple&#x201D; (2022) and &#x201C;Menus-Plaisirs, les Troisgros&#x201D; (2023).

&#x201C; Paper Tiger &#x201D; director James Gray has launched six of his nine feature films from the starry heights of the Cannes Film Festival , most recently contending for the Palme d&#x2019;Or this year with his New York-set crime drama.

Just don&#x2019;t expect to see him back on the Croisette anytime soon.

&#x201C;Cannes sucks. Don&#x2019;t worry, I'm not going back to Cannes,&#x201D; the director quipped Tuesday at the Marrakech Film Festival . &#x201C;I&#x2019;ve learned my lesson. Cannes is not for me. I am not for Cannes.&#x201D; blogherads.adq.push(function () { blogherads .defineSlot( 'medrec', 'gpt-variety-article-mid-article-uid0' ) .setTargeting( 'pos', ["mid-article1","mid-articleX","mid","mid-article"] ) .setTargeting( 'viewable', 'yes' ) .setSubAdUnitPath("ros\/mid-article") .addSize([[300,250],[2,2],[300,251],[2,4],[4,2],[320,480],[620,366],[300,450]]) .setClsOptimization("minsize") ; }); Related Stories Anthony Mackie and Jamie Dornan’s Heist Drama '12 12 12' Feels Like a Bad Video Game: TV Review

Appearing in conversation with Venice Film Festival director Alberto Barbera, the Queens-born filmmaker was speaking to a full house that included &#x201C;Artificial&#x201D; director Luca Guadagnino and screen icon and Marrakech tribute award recipient Jeff Goldblum.

Over the course of 90 freewheeling minutes, Gray delighted the audience with tales from his New York upbringing, opening up about his tussles with the Hollywood studios that refused to release his movies and offering his take on the often chilly critical responses to many of his films &#x2014; beginning with his audacious debut &#x201C;Little Odessa,&#x201D; which won a Silver Lion in Venice in 1994, when the director was just 25 years old.

"That&#x2019;s the history of movies. It takes 10 years for you to understand if it&#x2019;s anything at all. Right, Luca? Isn&#x2019;t that true? Nobody knows anything," he said. "They really don&#x2019;t know what the fuck they&#x2019;re talking about."

At the tail end of an audience Q&A, Gray was asked about the role that festival competitions play in the movie industry today. Though his tongue was partly planted in cheek as he trashed the prestigious French fest &#x2014; where he's never won an award &#x2014; the director didn&#x2019;t mince words as he ripped into the "idiotic" concept of pitting movies against each other. blogherads.adq.push(function () { blogherads .defineSlot( 'medrec', 'gpt-dsk-tab-mid-article2-uid1' ) .setTargeting( 'pos', ["mid","mid-article2","mid-articleX"] ) .setTargeting( 'viewable', 'yes' ) .setSubAdUnitPath("ros\/mid-article2") .addSize([[320,480],[300,250],[300,251],[2,4],[4,2],[620,366],[300,450]]) .setClsOptimization("minsize") ; });

&#x201C;I think the idea of the competition is terrible. I took the films [to Cannes] because the distributor wants it. They want that dumb logo on the film, but the idea is really dumb. We know that it&#x2019;s dumb,&#x201D; he said.

&#x201C;Euripides felt very bad because he wasn&#x2019;t winning a lot of prizes. It&#x2019;s true, by the way. He wound up living his life in a cave out of shame for not winning the prizes,&#x201D; Gray continued. &#x201C;I don&#x2019;t know who won the prizes during Euripides&#x2019; time. But the point is that I don&#x2019;t know who won the prizes. The whole thing is idiotic. It&#x2019;s not sports, you know?&#x201D;

The director was just warming up, directing his ire at the corporations that &#x201C;have done an excellent job at restricting access to a free flow of information and art.&#x201D;

&#x201C;What has the corporation done for us? 'You, shoot your movie in Atlanta. Shoot your movie in Budapest. Edit your movie in London.' Why? &#x2018;It&#x2019;s cheaper,&#x2019;&#x201D; said Gray. &#x201C;Not just because it's cheaper. Clusters of talent mean risk. Clusters of talent mean artists can gang up. Clusters of talent mean the New Hollywood, when a bunch of hippies ran the show, and they didn&#x2019;t like that at all. A cluster of talent means Fellini, Visconti, De Sica, Rossellini &#x2014; all those people working together. And the corporation doesn&#x2019;t like it. That&#x2019;s risk.&#x201D;

The director went on, saying, &#x201C;So what does the festival do? Communality. A bunch of filmmakers get together." He gestured to his pal Guadagnino, seated front and center in the audience. &#x201C;I see Luca. He&#x2019;s here in Marrakech. I can have dinner with him. He doesn&#x2019;t want to have dinner with me, maybe. But the point is that that communality is critical.

&#x201C;What is the thing in festivals that matters to the corporation? The competition. What wins. Why? That&#x2019;s the thing that&#x2019;s going to make them money,&#x201D; he continued. &#x201C;I hate the part where you compete. It&#x2019;s dumb; ethically, morally bankrupt. But it&#x2019;s also aiding and abetting the machine.&#x201D;

Instead, Gray celebrated film festivals as a space for &#x201C;the free-flowing exchange of ideas of thoughts" and championed them "as a communal thing, where we compare ideas and fight over films."

"&#x2018;I like that one. I hate that one.&#x2019; That's the coin of the realm. That is everything, and that's beautiful,&#x201D; he said. &#x201C;So anything that encourages a clustering of ideas, of thoughts, comparing and contrasting ideas: That is how we grow. To teach is also to learn. I think festivals are vitally important for that reason.&#x201D; blogherads.adq.push(function () { blogherads .defineSlot( 'medrec', 'gpt-variety-article-mid-articleX-uid2' ) .setTargeting( 'pos', ["btf","mid-articleX","mid"] ) .setTargeting( 'viewable', 'yes' ) .setSubAdUnitPath("ros\/mid-articleX") .addSize([[320,480],[300,250],[300,251],[620,366]]) .setClsOptimization("minsize") ; });

Fresh off an appearance at the Doha Film Festival , where &#x201C;Paper Tiger&#x201D; had its regional premiere, Gray has been making the rounds with his crime drama, which follows two brothers whose pursuit of the American Dream draws them into a dangerous scheme involving the Russian mafia. Starring Adam Driver, Miles Teller and Scarlett Johansson, the director&#x2019;s ninth feature was released theatrically by Neon earlier this month.

Gray is among the star-studded lineup participating in the Conversations series in Marrakech. Other A-listers appearing this week include screen stars John Turturro and Goldblum &#x2014; both recipients of tribute awards at the festival &#x2014; &#x201C;Knives Out&#x201D; director Rian Johnson, &#x201C;Artificial&#x201D; director Guadagnino and Italian screen icon Monica Bellucci.

The Marrakech Film Festival runs Nov. 20 &#x2013; 28.

James Marsden dominated social media buzz after Disney and Marvel Studios launched the final "Avengers: Doomsday" trailer , which ended on the viral moment of Marsden's Cyclops uniting the X-Men and Avengers in battle against Robert Downey Jr.'s Doctor Doom. Marsden event got to recite his character's iconic line: "To me, my X-Men!" Whether or not Marvel should've spoiled such a huge moment in the "Doomsday" trailer is now being widely debated among Marvel fans, but for Marsden it was moments like these that lured him back to playing Cyclops after 20 years. blogherads.adq.push(function () { blogherads .defineSlot( 'medrec', 'gpt-variety-article-mid-article-uid0' ) .setTargeting( 'pos', ["mid-article1","mid-articleX","mid","mid-article"] ) .setTargeting( 'viewable', 'yes' ) .setSubAdUnitPath("ros\/mid-article") .addSize([[300,250],[2,2],[300,251],[2,4],[4,2],[320,480],[620,366],[300,450]]) .setClsOptimization("minsize") ; }); Related Stories Anthony Mackie and Jamie Dornan’s Heist Drama '12 12 12' Feels Like a Bad Video Game: TV Review

"One of the things people have said for years is that Cyclops is a leader, yet in many of the previous films he often took a back seat to Wolverine and some of the other characters," Marsden told Sharp magazine in a profile that published the same day as the "Doomsday" final trailer launch.

"There are only so many minutes available in a film this large, but it was important to me that my return felt meaningful," he continued. "I didn&#x2019;t want Cyclops to simply appear for a nostalgic cameo and then disappear. I wanted there to be a genuine purpose behind his presence. Without giving anything away, I feel very good about what we were able to do with the character.&#x201D;

Marsden debuted as Scott Summers/Cyclops in 2000&#x2019;s &#x201C;X-Men&#x201D; and reprised the role in 2003&#x2019;s &#x201C;X2: X-Men United&#x201D; and 2006&#x2019;s &#x201C;X-Men: The Last Stand.&#x201D; The character was killed off in the latter film, as Marsden moved on to film &#x201C;Superman Returns.&#x201D; But now Cyclops is back for &#x201C;Doomsday&#x201D; and leading the X-Men crew, which includes his original co-stars such as Patrick Stewart (Charles Xavier), Ian McKellen (Magneto), Kelsey Grammer (Beast), Alan Cumming (Nightcrawler) and Rebecca Romijn (Mystique). blogherads.adq.push(function () { blogherads .defineSlot( 'medrec', 'gpt-dsk-tab-mid-article2-uid1' ) .setTargeting( 'pos', ["mid","mid-article2","mid-articleX"] ) .setTargeting( 'viewable', 'yes' ) .setSubAdUnitPath("ros\/mid-article2") .addSize([[320,480],[300,250],[300,251],[2,4],[4,2],[620,366],[300,450]]) .setClsOptimization("minsize") ; });

Why did " Avengers: Doomsday " narrow in on these X-Men and not others such as Halle Berry&#x2019;s Storm or Anna Paquin&#x2019;s Rogue? Co-director Joe Russo recently told Entertainment Weekly the casting decisions were "really targeted. It was really specific."

&#x201C;We really do have a process where we see the entire film through each character&#x2019;s eyes, no matter what the size of their role is,&#x201D; Anthony Russo added.. &#x201C;With the X-Men, we got to really deep dive and think about their histories as characters, their experiences, and how this particular moment in time was gonna affect them. There&#x2019;s such a rich history to them that we really do bring them to the film as if it&#x2019;s their movie, as well.&#x201D;

"Avengers: Doomsday" opens in theaters Dec. 18.

The horror satire &#x201C; Namaslay &#x201D; will be available to stream on Apple TV, Amazon, Fandango at Home and Google Pay on Dec. 15.

Directed by brothers Kanish Arhant-Sudhir and Rish Arhant-Sudhir, their feature film debut follows a grieving woman, Gayatri (Kirunthuja Srikanth-Talim), who is invited by her friend Judy (Angela Sant&#x2019;Albano) to an upscale yoga studio to to reconnect with the yoga traditions she inherited from her late grandmother. The result is a fiery conversation about the appropriation of yoga in the West, proving culture is the blood that keeps the past alive. blogherads.adq.push(function () { blogherads .defineSlot( 'medrec', 'gpt-variety-article-mid-article-uid0' ) .setTargeting( 'pos', ["mid-article1","mid-articleX","mid","mid-article"] ) .setTargeting( 'viewable', 'yes' ) .setSubAdUnitPath("ros\/mid-article") .addSize([[300,250],[2,2],[300,251],[2,4],[4,2],[320,480],[620,366],[300,450]]) .setClsOptimization("minsize") ; }); Related Stories Anthony Mackie and Jamie Dornan’s Heist Drama '12 12 12' Feels Like a Bad Video Game: TV Review

&#x201C;We&#x2019;re thrilled to bring &#x2018;Namaslay&#x2019; to an even wider audience through its digital release,&#x201D; Rish and Kanish said in a statement. &#x201C;We made this film to be experienced, shared and talked about and we&#x2019;re excited that audiences across the country will have the opportunity to discover the world we created. As we continue our awards campaign, we&#x2019;re grateful to everyone who has supported the film and look forward to its next chapter with audiences wherever they watch.&#x201D;

To develop the meaningful story they wanted to share with audiences, the brothers turned inward to their real relationships and families&#x2019; lived experiences.

&#x201C;There&#x2019;s something that&#x2019;s truly slapstick almost about the whole experience, but then there&#x2019;s also something beneath that&#x2019;s kind of sinister,&#x201D; Rish said during the Variety Screening Series panel . &#x201C;It&#x2019;s a lot of strains of colonialism, there&#x2019;s commoditization that&#x2019;s happening, there is an extraction and then a resale at a premium.&#x201D; blogherads.adq.push(function () { blogherads .defineSlot( 'medrec', 'gpt-dsk-tab-mid-article2-uid1' ) .setTargeting( 'pos', ["mid","mid-article2","mid-articleX"] ) .setTargeting( 'viewable', 'yes' ) .setSubAdUnitPath("ros\/mid-article2") .addSize([[320,480],[300,250],[300,251],[2,4],[4,2],[620,366],[300,450]]) .setClsOptimization("minsize") ; });

Kanish echoed, &#x201C;An identity is not a story. It&#x2019;s a part of a character that affects how they interact with a story, and there are a lot of movies that have characters who have various identities that are not palpable at all, but the identity of a character in and of itself is not enough to undergird a narrative.&#x201D;

Alongside Srikanth-Talim and Sant&#x2019;Albano, &#x201C;Namaslay&#x201D; stars Alicia Mitchell-Mangual, Usha Krishnan and Christina Moore. The film is produced by Venk Potula via Khrisp Entertainment, alongside producers Rish and Kanish through their independent film studio Junghal Studios.
